  "answer_core": "Do not choose a dissertation direction yet. Treat the next couple of weeks as a short probe. Your decision hinges on two gates: whether the Silva data path is real, and whether your original fallback path is still fully viable.\n\nGate 1 (Silva): Confirm whether there is concrete data you can access on a clear timeline, what work would be yours, what authorship/collaboration terms look like, and whether your advisor explicitly supports you pursuing this without pulling you back to the safer lab path. Get only the information needed to verify data access and collaboration depth; do not build a full proposal.\n\nGate 2 (Fallback): Check that the fallback remains advisor‑backed, resourced, technically ready, and able to carry a dissertation if the Silva path fails. Set a visible stop date and conditions for saying no to Silva if the gate fails.\n\nSequence: Speak with your advisor first. Use Dr. Silva only for low‑cost, concrete checks about data and timelines. Talk to the committee only after you and your advisor know whether the Silva path is real and whether the fallback remains protected.\n\nDo not run all options in parallel. Make the final direction choice only after both gates return actual evidence within your defined short window.",
